   "design": "A phone till app ({OTHER}) linked to a card reader records each sale with the stop it was made at, so the sales and leftovers record and most of the cash count fall away. From that history and the event calendar, it suggests the next day's load per item for the driver to adjust; driving and selling stay as they are.",
   "previous_blocker": "Sales were cash and notes, so there was no history to plan loads from.",
   "enabler_now": "Phone till apps with card readers are cheap and record sales per place and time.",
   "still_hard": "Weather and match results change demand; the suggestion is only a start.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing the regulars by name and what they want before they ask.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Nothing changes; loading is better informed and the cash count shorter.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "food truck owner",
     "task": "Plan stock for events",
     "learn": "Whether sales history per stop cuts leftovers."
    }
   ],
